==========================================
DAY 09 NOTES — Package Management
Date: 05-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- apt = high-level tool (handles repos + dependencies), dpkg = low-level tool (installs .deb files)
- apt update ONLY refreshes the package catalog, doesn't install anything
- apt upgrade actually installs newer versions of already-installed software
- apt remove keeps config files, apt purge deletes them too
- apt autoremove cleans up leftover unused dependencies
- Installing via official repos = signed, trusted packages
- Random .sh install scripts from the internet bypass this trust — risky

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] apt update / apt upgrade
[ ] apt search / apt show
[ ] apt install / apt list --installed
[ ] apt remove vs apt purge
[ ] dpkg -l

fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ sudo apt update
> 

$ sudo apt install tree
> 

$ apt list --installed | grep tree
> 


